# Guild Life Adventures - Environment Variables
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your values.
# .env.local is gitignored and never committed.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PARTYKIT (optional: public lobby service + community world ranking)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# PartyKit provides persistent server storage for the optional community
# world ranking. The ranking is labelled "unverified" because gameplay is
# client-authoritative; PartyKit validates ranges and rate-limits submissions,
# but cannot prove that a browser did not modify its own score.
#
# The repository also contains a PartyKit public-room listing service. The
# current browser lobby uses MQTT by default, so room-code multiplayer still
# works when PartyKit is not configured.
#
# Setup steps:
#   1. Install the CLI:  npm install -g partykit   (or use npx)
#   2. Login:            npx partykit login
#   3. Deploy:           npx partykit deploy
#      → You get a URL like: guild-life-adventures.<your-name>.partykit.dev
#   4. Set VITE_PARTYKIT_HOST below (without https://)
#
# For local development:
#   Run:  npx partykit dev
#   Then: VITE_PARTYKIT_HOST=localhost:1999
#
# If not set, world ranking is disabled gracefully and the local Hall of Fame
# continues to work. Players can still host/join games by room code.
#
VITE_PARTYKIT_HOST=guild-life-adventures.your-username.partykit.dev

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PEERJS (optional — for self-hosted PeerJS server with discovery)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# If you self-host a PeerJS server with --allow_discovery, set the URL here.
# Example: npx peerjs --port 9000 --allow_discovery
# VITE_PEERJS_HOST=http://localhost:9000

# For GitHub Actions deployment, add these as repository secrets and reference them in your workflow.
